Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Annibale kernel maintainers
Description:
		Experimental read-only integer telemetry for the Annibale master
		gauge (ti,bq27z561_master, I2C address 0x55, ic_role 0).
		Each read performs one SMBus word transaction. Voltage is mV;
		current is microamps, positive on discharge, negative on charge
		(the MCA convention). Temperatures are tenths of degrees Celsius.
		Charge values are microamp-hours; SOC/SOH are integer percentages;
		cycle_count is an integer count. Internal temperature is the gauge
		internal sensor, not a second pack sensor. SOC is raw gauge SOC,
		not smoothed Android UI capacity. Reads are not an atomic snapshot.
		Bus errors propagate, out-of-range values return ERANGE, suspended
		reads return EHOSTDOWN and teardown returns ENODEV. No cached or
		fabricated replacement values are returned. These are diagnostic
		interfaces, not charging-control or battery-authentication APIs.
